=== CONTRACT goal-gate "MEASUREMENT TRUTH item 2 — THE SENDER CPU CEILING (PRE-REGISTRATION, PHASE 1)"
=== ARMS  B = no instrument (THE CEILING'S OWN ARM) | S = RWM_CPUPROF=1 (self-timing) | P = perf record -p <client> on the release-prof build
=== THE CEILING'S ms/MB IS READ OFF ARM B AND OFF NOTHING ELSE. An instrument that costs CPU at a CPU-BOUND cell moves the number it reports; B is what bounds that, and S-vs-B and P-vs-B ARE the instrument-cost measurement.
=== NO DIAG/ACKDIAG/WALLDIAG/LATPROBE ON ANY ARM — all of them are sender-side costs inside the quantity under decomposition. This env DIFFERS from the era and latency batteries deliberately.
=== perf attaches by PID, selected on '--client' in /proc/<pid>/cmdline. Both roles are the same executable; recency would race.
=== perf's ATTACH GAP is recorded per invocation (attach_ms). P is read as a SHAPE, never as a total; the total is B's CPUCLI.
